        {
          "id": "SP_PELLICIERA_BENTHAMII_CORNEJO",
          "name": "Pelliciera benthamii  Cornejo",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "lineage": "Pelliciera",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Pelliciera benthamii Cornejo — a neotropical mangrove tree recently elevated from varietal to species rank (Cornejo & Bonifaz, 2020) based on genetic, morphological, and ecological evidence. Distinguished from P. rhizophorae by pink to crimson-red floral bracts (vs white/cream), smaller stature resembling a dwarf version, and dentate leaf margins. Native to the Caribbean coast from Panama to northern Colombia, occupying the understory of Rhizophora-dominated mangroves in low-salinity zones. Flowers are large, showy, pentamerous, visited by hummingbirds and potentially bats; fruits are viviparous propagules.",
          "sourcedFrom": "websearch",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "ca1f098f-6da9-599-888-1dd047c43b9518",
          "sourceIds": {
