          },
          "authorityIds": "col:55P7M,wfo:wfo-0000456184",
          "description": "Tetramerista glabra Miq. — an evergreen mid-canopy tree reaching up to 37 m tall with a fluted base, small buttresses, and leathery, glabrous leaves with marginal pit-glands. Native to western Malesia (Sumatra, Peninsular Malaysia, Borneo), where it grows in freshwater and peat swamp forests, mangroves, and mixed dipterocarp forests up to 200 m altitude. Flowers tetramerous, greenish-yellow to golden, 13–25 mm across, borne in axillary panicles. Fruit a round berry 15–30 mm wide, green to purple, with edible sour pulp; seeds oblong, 10–15 mm. Wood is light yellow-brown with pink tinges, used for fencing, planks, posts, and firewood. Also known locally as Entuyut or Punah.",
          "authorship": "Miquel, 1861",
          "authorIds": [
            "Q76742"
          ]
